    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "00284184-6e55-5a49-858c-2b998129eaa0",
      ":question/problem": "Find ${y}^{\\prime}$ for $y=e^{- 7 x} \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}.$\n\n| ${y}^{\\prime}$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $x e^{7 x}$ |",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}$ and the denominator $v(x)=e^{7 x}.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\nu'(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\quad v'(x)=7 e^{7 x}.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\\prime} & =\\frac{u'(x)v(x)-u(x)v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2} \\\\ & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})(e^{7 x})-(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})(7 e^{7 x})}{(e^{7 x})^2} \\\\ & =- \\frac{\\left(7 x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} - 1\\right) e^{- 7 x}}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "1c1f80f1-267a-5b70-ab6c-937f84ce98be",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "ad6dbdba-d35d-5c59-a8ec-0feaf774a414"
          ],
